---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { school } from "../data/school";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy — ${school.shortName}`}
  description={`How the ${school.shortName} website handles information: the admission enquiry form stores nothing — details go only into a WhatsApp message you review and send yourself.`}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container privacy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>What this website does with your information.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Written in plain language, because it should be.</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not store your information. There is no database, no
        account system, no analytics tracker, and no cookie banner because
        there is nothing to consent to.
      </p>

      <h2>The admission enquiry form</h2>
      <p>
        When you fill in the enquiry form, everything you type stays on your
        own device while you complete it. Nothing is sent to this website's
        servers, saved in your browser for later, or shared with any third
        party.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you choose <strong>Continue on WhatsApp</strong>, your details are
        placed into a prepared WhatsApp message. You see the full message in
        WhatsApp before it goes anywhere, and it is only sent if you press send
        yourself. From that point the conversation is between you and the
        school on WhatsApp, covered by WhatsApp's own terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose to call instead, no form information leaves your device
        at all.
      </p>

      <h2>What we deliberately do not ask for</h2>
      <p>
        The enquiry form does not ask for a child's date of birth, Aadhaar
        number, documents, photographs, medical details, or home address. A
        first enquiry does not need them; the school will ask for whatever is
        required later, directly.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Buttons for WhatsApp, phone, Instagram and Google Maps open those apps
        or sites. Each is run by its own company under its own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Ask the school office directly — call <a href={school.phoneHref}>{school.phoneDisplay}</a> or message on <a href={school.whatsappBase} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="privacy__note">
        This notice describes how the website currently works. If the school
        later adds a form that stores enquiries, this page will be updated
        first and the change will require school approval.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .privacy__note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--red);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
